figdown 0.1 block
# 0.1 (`LINK-OPERATOR-IN-IDS`): `--` is the LINK OPERATOR, so it may not also occur
# inside an id. While it could, `bundle t1 a-x--b` had two legal readings and
# the greedy member regex silently committed to one, making the other
# unreachable (RULE 6.3: malformed input is an error, never a guess).
# The ban also settles the whitespace disagreement: `edge a--b` now means the
# same thing `bundle t1 a--b` does.
node a "A"
node b "B"
edge a--b
node x--y "Double dash in a node id"
class c--1 "meaning"
# `plane l--1` stood here until 0.3 — the whole directive left the
# language (`PAINT-ORDER-CONSTRUCT`), so that id position left with it.

figdown 0.1 topology
# Section 2: the `bundle` half, which is the half `LINK-OPERATOR-IN-IDS` was
# written for — `bundle` is now declared by `topology` only (`SCENE-KEYWORD-MEMBERSHIP`), so the
# lines moved here rather than being deleted. Losing them would leave the
# rule pinned only on the ids that never had two readings, and the greedy
# member regex is the whole reason the ban exists.
node a "A"
node b "B"
edge a--b
bundle ok a--b
bundle t--1 "L" a--b
bundle t2 "L" a--b--a
